<article class="env-remark" id="0FVE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FVE">Remark <span data-tag="0FVE">42.43.2</span>.</a> The proof of Lemma <a href="/tag/02UL" data-tag="02UL">42.43.1</a> shows that the morphism $\pi : P \to X$ has the following additional properties: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\pi $ is a finite composition of projective space bundles associated to locally free modules of finite constant rank, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for every $\alpha \in \mathop{\mathrm{CH}}\nolimits _ k(X)$ we have $\alpha = \pi _*(\xi _1 \cap \ldots \cap \xi _ d \cap \pi ^*\alpha )$ where $\xi _ i$ is the first Chern class of some invertible $\mathcal{O}_ P$-module. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> The second observation follows from the first and Lemma <a href="/tag/02TW" data-tag="02TW">42.36.1</a>. We will add more observations here as needed. </p>
</article>